{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty","id":814460,"title":"Questions about Majesty","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T14:42:24-08:00","id":814460,"title":"Questions about Majesty","content":"Currently running a vampire game and a few players are feeling like Majesty is OP. I'm running a vampire 2ed<br /> <br /> What kind can someone have vs Majesty. For some reason my players believe the whole lashing out thing is a violent action that will make people attack them. From reading it I keep seeing lashing out as just your Aura is stronger than theirs.<br /> <br /> So my question is what kind of defense can you have vs Majesty other than lashing out<br /> <br /> Also is Lashing out a violent action that can make people attack you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T15:01:49-08:00","id":814473,"title":"","content":"Might I ask what the context of the Majesty usage is? Because while Lashing Out is generally an aggressive action, so is booming out a 'love me' field at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T15:24:23-08:00","id":814484,"title":"","content":"Lashing Out is basically just posturing. It's not inherently violent, but it is a challenge, and different people will react to a challenge in different ways. The Monsterous Beast is by far the most likely to lead to physical confrontation, since it's the vampire equivalent of taking off your shirt and saying &quot;come at me, bro!&quot; But even that is just a nonviolent display of dominance more often than not. The Seductive Beast is like an agressive come-on. Might get you laid, might get you an eye roll, might get you laughed at and a drink thrown in your face. Probably won't get you physically attacked, but you never know.<br /> The Competitive Beast is like a &quot;bet I can [do a thing] better than you.&quot; It's far more likely to lead to a [do a thing] competition than a physical fight, unless [do a thing] happens to be bareknuckle boxing. But, you know, some people don't take kindly to boasting and some people don't deal well with losing a challenge, especially to a braggart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-22-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T15:29:13-08:00","id":814489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=814473#post814473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I ask what the context of the Majesty usage is? Because while Lashing Out is generally an aggressive action, so is booming out a 'love me' field at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kindred doing it in there own club to draw in humans. Then an elder using to try and charm a player to let them feed on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T15:48:51-08:00","id":814505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=814489#post814489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred doing it in there own club to draw in humans. Then an elder using to try and charm a player to let them feed on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it just the first dot they have problems with? Because that alone won't force them to kowtow to the Elder's every whim. At best it will stop them from begrudging him the request, perhaps even make him seem like a cool, opportunistic guy...until he leaves and they have some time to think on it. If they need it Lashing Out is there for a reason, and can easily be played off in self defense. If they are afraid of getting attack for trying to resist mind-control you might remind them that mind control <b>is </b>an attack, and arguably a worse one than physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T05:02:23-08:00","id":814787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty#post814460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently running a vampire game and a few players are feeling like Majesty is OP. I'm running a vampire 2ed</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Kindred doing it in there own club to draw in humans. Then an elder using to try and charm a player to let them feed on them.</span> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Can I ask why they feel its overpowered? I don't think that drawing mortals to feed on them is exactly overpowered. Dominate 1 can take any person, get them to do anything, and make their memory say that they wanted to do it.<br /> <br /> An elder using Majesty is a pretty powerful issue, but -elder vampire-. They're supposed to be scary powerful with the mind control. Charm has a drawback that a significant personal sacrifice (feeding may likely count) Resolves the Condition and makes you distrustful. <br /> <br /> Is it possible your PCs are reacting to the general boost in power of 2e? Majesty, Dominate, and Nightmare are all scarily strong now. Usually when I see someone complain about something being overpowered, its because of the new power level of 2e being so much higher and not being used to it.<br /> <br /> Maybe its a reaction to being the target of a mind-control effect? I see players not take well to it.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T09:44:26-08:00","id":814888,"title":"","content":"I think Awe is not so powerful. Majesty start to be powerful with Green Eyes and Loyalty. But, for example, Idol, is really strong against ancillae and neonates but it's not too much useful vs other elder vampire, even if it is used by an elder. Cause the potential enemy must to roll Blood Potency + Resolve minus Majesty (5). So for an elder (BP 5 or more) the dice pool to acts against the Majesty users is enough to have a success in the most part of the rolls.<br /> <br /> In my opinion it's unbalanced respect the tirhd and fourth level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:52:48-08:00","id":815271,"title":"","content":"I believe it says somewhere that you should have a good reason to lash out against awe because awe is subtle. It is so subtle people don't know they are under the effects of it. So it you're playing and your player says &quot; I kick on awe for my turn&quot; and everyone else says &quot;I lash out in response&quot; or every Npc lashes out it totally takes away from what majesty is. If everyone knows it's being used on them, that means mortals would too. Idol is really powerful against non-elders. But elders get a decent resist and might even get the chance to lash out. Idol only words if awe worked. <br /> <br /> Charm is no more or less powerful than mesmerize though enthrall means these guys would take a bullet for you. <br /> <br /> I think it's balanced vs nightmare and dominate and the rest. But if your players aren't equipped to To &quot;fight&quot; mental attacks, then yeah it can seem OP. <br /> <br /> Lashing out is an attack. It forces fight or flight. And depending on which you chose some nasty things. Use the seductive lash and charm. You could tempt them into oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T01:11:08-08:00","id":815306,"title":"","content":"On NPCs making your PCs doing something: remember that the Social Maneuvering system is explicitly -not- for use against PCs, so unless the ST really starts pushing social mechanics then Awe can't -force- you to do anything, it just makes someone extremely charming and persuasive. If it gets further up into Majesty where it -is- forcing you to do something, I think it's entirely in line to Lash Out. No fair judge would hold that measure of self defense against you, but then again if it's an elder it might not -be- a fair judge.<br /> <br /> If your players still feel it's an issue, then direct them to the Composure attribute, and maybe consider temporarily upping the beats per session so they can grab Composure without feeling like it's taking up all their xp, or give them a cost break, or hell, just give them some free dots if you want. Totally up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T04:05:02-08:00","id":815348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=815306#post815306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On NPCs making your PCs doing something: remember that the Social Maneuvering system is explicitly -not- for use against PCs</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. The mechanics explicitly have a separate part against using them against PCs, and allowing for alternatives and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T05:46:04-08:00","id":815378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=815306#post815306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On NPCs making your PCs doing something: remember that the Social Maneuvering system is explicitly -not- for use against PCs,</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that 1) the GMC book provides ways to use Social Maneuvering on other PCs (the words they use is &quot;unfair&quot;), and 2) Majesty 2 kinda bypasses the whole need for Social Maneuvering in a lot of cases. When you're Charmed, you willingly do favors for him as if he was a best friend.<br /> <br /> <br /> What you're ignoring is that the Social Maneuvering system suggests that using it on PCs is unfair, and that it should be roleplayed out. In a realistic scenario, however, <i>roleplaying things out should generally end up with the same result as if you used social maneuvering.</i> If someone Charms you, then you should roleplay out being charmed, as if the person is your best friend. What's a little bite between best friends? Letting us crash together for a night? <br /> <br /> That line about not using S.M. on players isn't an instant out to ignore an NPC's social efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-24-2016, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:08:06-08:00","id":815576,"title":"","content":"Mm. The PC resolutions in GMC are okay, but very much optional. In the meantime, I'm going off the explicit message of &quot;this system is meant for PCs to use on NPCs&quot; found in GMC, VtR2 and WtF2.<br /> <br /> I largely agree that roleplaying efforts shouldn't be &quot;ignored&quot;, but what that means differs from table to table. It's the old question of &quot;does using the Diplomacy skill make a PC&quot; do something&quot; that's been around since social mechanics were introduced in RPGs, and at my table I very explicitly separate mundane charm and mind control. So while I can try to make a roleplayed offer as compelling as possible, describe the NPC as being smoother and sweeter than ice cream and otherwise argue about it until I am blue in the face, the PCs have the option to say no.<br /> <br /> Does that give the players a somewhat meta level of rationality that people in the real world often don't have when accosted by charmers, salesmen and flim flam artists? Well...yes, and I would tell my players that's how I handle social stuff before the game even begins, because it's a big deal to me. Ideally I want players to give up some of their agency but I'm not going to take it from them. <br /> <br /> Once you get into Majesty, you're falling into the softer side of straight up mind control, which is another story entirely and, for me, falls in that grey area in Kindred society where you can legitimately argue that it's use is offensive or at the very least aggressive in nature and that measures like lashing out is a matter of self defense. <br /> <br /> Now, I am not saying that this whole wall of text is the best way to play, but I am offering it up as food for thought in a thread where OP's PCs are struggling with how Majesty makes them do stuff since I put a lot of thought into it for my own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:17:29-08:00","id":815581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=815576#post815576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm. The PC resolutions in GMC are okay, but very much optional. In the meantime, I'm going off the explicit message of &amp;quot;this system is meant for PCs to use on NPCs&amp;quot; found in GMC, VtR2 and WtF2.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely true. I do think it's worth noting, however, that the sidebar from GMC that said Social Maneuvering isn't meant to be used on PCs was removed from CofD, but the part about letting PCs take a Condition and offer an alternative stayed. Also, there are a few Merits that are useless to PCs if Social Maneuvering isn't used on them, so if you're not going to allow Social Maneuvering against PCs, you should probably warn your players so they know not to take Closed Book or Table Turner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:56:01-08:00","id":815701,"title":"","content":"Not just a few merits, but several powers explicitly won't work when used on PCs without Social Maneuvering. I get the feeling that the whole &quot;unfair to use on PCs&quot; is derived from that same &quot;does diplomacy make a PC do something&quot; argument, just from people on the other side of the fence. I find it rather notable that the justification for Social Maneuvering being &quot;unfair&quot; is because a PC can't say &quot;no.&quot; However, the GMC rules say the very first thing - decide if its reasonable, if not, say &quot;no.&quot; So, very much saying no is part of the default assumption of the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T15:03:43-08:00","id":815707,"title":"","content":"Yeah. If a character <i>could </i>be convinced to do something, then it's grounds for social maneuvering. My personal advice to players is to err on the side of &quot;Yes&quot; in these situations. It's interesting, generates plot <i>and </i>is gonna net you more Beats! It's a situation where everyone wins!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:13:37-08:00","id":815886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=815707#post815707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. If a character <i>could </i>be convinced to do something, then it's grounds for social maneuvering. My personal advice to players is to err on the side of &quot;Yes&quot; in these situations. It's interesting, generates plot <i>and </i>is gonna net you more Beats! It's a situation where everyone wins!</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. If you have a particularly charming NPC trying to persuade a character, dangle beats in front of your players. If they say 'yes', they get a beat. If they say 'no', they don't get a beat. The option is always theirs, but don't be afraid to dangle a carrot in front of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:36:23-08:00","id":815891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=815701#post815701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just a few merits, but several powers explicitly won't work when used on PCs without Social Maneuvering. I get the feeling that the whole &quot;unfair to use on PCs&quot; is derived from that same &quot;does diplomacy make a PC do something&quot; argument, just from people on the other side of the fence. I find it rather notable that the justification for Social Maneuvering being &quot;unfair&quot; is because a PC can't say &quot;no.&quot; However, the GMC rules say the very first thing - decide if its reasonable, if not, say &quot;no.&quot; So, very much saying no is part of the default assumption of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a significant difference between something being refused because it's wholly unreasonable and something being refused even if it's reasonable and tempting. If the version that you used on PCs had no alterations, then that would mean that a PC with all his Doors opened would have to do anything that wasn't patently unacceptable by any means by the ST's standards.<br /> <br /> The ability to offer an alternative listed in GMC is an decent solution, but all in all I'm not really sold on the idea anyways. I like Doors as a bookkeeping measure for NPCs, but as something that PCs have to track, it starts getting complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:11:44-08:00","id":816024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=815891#post815891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a significant difference between something being refused because it's wholly unreasonable and something being refused even if it's reasonable and tempting. If the version that you used on PCs had no alterations, then that would mean that a PC with all his Doors opened would have to do anything that wasn't patently unacceptable by any means by the ST's standards.<br /> <br /> The ability to offer an alternative listed in GMC is an decent solution, but all in all I'm not really sold on the idea anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div> Between saying no, the alternative option, and the sheer time and opertunities involved in needing to open Doors, I find that its a lot less of an issue that you're making it out to be. If a player doesn't want to do something, there's so many ways to not have it happen. I've found that the spector of anything potentially touching player agency is more of an issue than the actual reality execution of it.<br /> <br /> Realistically, if someone is using powers or skills to sway characters, then, by all rights, the characters should be swayed. Too often, I see the idea that PCs <i>can't</i> be swayed in anyway by mechanics as an excuse to be effectively immune to anything shy of Dominate-style magic. One character gets an exceptional success on a speech to evoke emotion, and a PC shrugs it off as of no consequence. Someone uses Majesty to influence emotions and wanting to give favors, and the PC shrugs it off and flatly refuses, goes on with the daily life as if no magic was there.<br /> <br /> That above is really my big issue with our discussion. You're suggesting that Majesty can't make you do anything, and at higher levels, it should be blindingly obvious to the point that its almost a given to Lash Out. Nevermind that the power itself says that players don't feel cheated, and the devs have said that Majesty is subtle enough that its not obvious that Lashing Out is a given. &quot;No judge will hold that self defefnse against you.&quot; No judge would see it as self defense, because the Lash Out was the first attack! <br /> <br /> Also, something that no one commented on that first responce you made.... <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your players still feel it's an issue, then direct them to the Composure attribute, and maybe consider temporarily upping the beats per session so they can grab Composure without feeling like it's taking up all their xp, or give them a cost break, or hell, just give them some free dots if you want. Totally up to you. </div> </div> </div> Resolve. Resolve is the attribute for resting Majesty now, not Composure. As well, there's the Indominable merit, and most games have some kind of mental shield option (Carthian Law, Mind 2 shielding, Fearless Hunter off the top of my head). Vampires also have the option of Riding the Wave, which shrugs off virtually all mental magic save very specific applications.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-25-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:53:29-08:00","id":816039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816024#post816024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Vampires also have the option of Riding the Wave, which shrugs off virtually all mental magic save very specific applications.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>It has always been my interpretation that Riding the Wave can only be used as a response to Frenzy, not to initiate it any time one likes. Voluntary Frenzy is the purview of the Coil of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I largely agree with the rest, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:18:33-08:00","id":816047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816039#post816039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has always been my interpretation that Riding the Wave can only be used as a response to Frenzy, not to initiate it any time one likes. Voluntary Frenzy is the purview of the Coil of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I largely agree with the rest, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Riding the Wave can be done any time... it's not a response to frenzy, it's too late if you've triggered frenzy normally. Coil of the Wyrm just makes it a lot easier and allows you to do it in response to normal frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:50:32-08:00","id":816104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816047#post816047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riding the Wave can be done any time... it's not a response to frenzy, it's too late if you've triggered frenzy normally. Coil of the Wyrm just makes it a lot easier and allows you to do it in response to normal frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's....just not true...at all. Riding the wave is always in response to a provocation. You can't just initialise it at will. It's an alternative to resisting frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:31:57-08:00","id":816131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816104#post816104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's....just not true...at all. Riding the wave is always in response to a provocation. You can't just initialise it at will. It's an alternative to resisting frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div> The book, at no point, says that. <br /> <br /> &quot;Some Kindred choose to grab their Beasts by the reins, and wield that monstrous power. It\u2019s a risky proposition, but one with great rewards. This practice is called riding the wave of frenzy.<br /> To ride the wave, spend a Willpower point, and make the normal Resolve + Composure resistance roll.&quot; <br /> <br /> To ride the wave, you spend willpower and roll. At no point is &quot;instead of a regular roll, you can do this&quot; or any variation thereof mentioned. Its just telling you how to enter the Wave. <br /> <br /> The main section dealing with provocations says, &quot;Either she\u2019ll force it down, or the Beast overwhelms her to fight, feed, or flee.&quot; Nothing about riding the wave here either.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but there's no supporting evidence for the idea that Riding the Wave must be in responce to outside provocation. I mean, its easy to justify that intial willpower expendature as dragging up anger or hunger and focusing on it while leashing the Beast enough to do the job, effectively provoking yourself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T09:13:41-08:00","id":816156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To ride the wave, spend a Willpower point, and make the<br /> normal Resolve + Composure resistance roll. The Willpower<br /> point does not add to this roll.<b> Success holds off the frenzy for<br /> a turn</b> as if she\u2019d spent Willpower to fight the frenzy. She can<br /> continue to do this until she fails, runs out of Willpower, or<br /> until she accumulates five successes. Treat any failure on this<br /> roll as a dramatic failure. </div> </div> </div>How are you holding off Frenzy for a turn if there's nothing to hold off yet?<br /> <br /> You resist or you Ride or you give in, in response to a Frenzy trigger.<br /> <br /> If you can just Ride whenever, there's no point to Coil of the Wyrm's &quot;enter Frenzy whenever you want&quot; Coils. It's heavily implied if not directly stated.<br /> <br /> Also see the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, you may choose the Beast\u2019s desire and specific target<br /> at the outset. <b>This desire does not have to align with the<br /> provocation.</b> For example, if Victoria risks frenzy because she\u2019s<br /> starved, she might choose to kill Dominic instead of feeding. </div> </div> </div>There has to be provocation. Just like normal Frenzy.<br /> <br /> It's also called &quot;riding the wave of frenzy.&quot; How can you ride a wave that doesn't exist?<br /> <br /> One of the Coils of the Wyrm:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When<br /> he enters frenzy the Dragon may opt to forego all resistance,<br /> falling into a state that will not cease until the Beast is sated<br /> <b>(though he may still ride the wave)</b>. </div> </div> </div>When a vampire enters Frenzy with this Coil, he can't resist, but he can <b>still</b> Ride the Wave. Still. As in, that's a standard potential response to Frenzy. Not something granted by the Coil.<br /> <br /> You may not find the evidence sufficient, you may not like that this interpretation weakens your Frenzy build or whatever, but saying there is no evidence to support this interpretation is patently false.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:45:07-08:00","id":816255,"title":"","content":"Quick answer right now, trying to hit the important bits but will be more brief than normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816024#post816024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found that the spector of anything potentially touching player agency is more of an issue than the actual reality execution of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, the discussion we're having is largely one about design and gameplay, making a mountain of the molehill it usually is in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Realistically, if someone is using powers or skills to sway characters, then, by all rights, the characters should be swayed. Too often, I see the idea that PCs <i>can't</i> be swayed in anyway by mechanics as an excuse to be effectively immune to anything shy of Dominate-style magic. </div> </div> </div>Correct. If you make the Diplomacy question a binary &quot;yes/no&quot; choice then I fall on the side that says that the PCs can ignore it, because the opposite is that they <i>can't</i>. Rephrased, in situations involving social mechanics, that means that at best what a character does is up to the whims of the dice and at worst the guys with the bigger pools can bully a character into doing something they don't want to or never would do.<br /> <br /> This is why binary &quot;yes/no&quot; social mechanics suck when aimed at PCs! It's also why the important and fun bits of modern social mechanics center around this dilemma, often breaking the binary, working with incentives, etc. to make it interesting. The CofD version of offering Beats if you give in is a good attempt at making bad choices palatable, and coming up with an alternative and taking a condition is an okay mechanic (if a bit clunky and not really exciting) that's pretty much the bare minimum for making a &quot;you refuse, but...&quot; option. I don't really have a problem with these parts of the social maneuvering system when it comes to PCs - like I said, it's pretty much when it comes down to the longer term Impressions and Doors part that makes it awkward and obtuse for me, to the point that I'm just not going to use it! I'll either stick to roleplaying with one-off rolls giving a metric for how strongly an argument resonates with you, and probably offer Beats to incentivize successful rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're suggesting that Majesty can't make you do anything, and at higher levels, it should be blindingly obvious to the point that its almost a given to Lash Out. Nevermind that the power itself says that players don't feel cheated, and the devs have said that Majesty is subtle enough that its not obvious that Lashing Out is a given. &quot;No judge will hold that self defefnse against you.&quot; No judge would see it as self defense, because the Lash Out was the first attack! </div> </div> </div>I never said that Majesty didn't do anything (at worst, you could argue that I said that Awe is &quot;useless&quot; against PCs) or that it was &quot;blindingly obvious&quot; and that Lashing Out is a given. What I'm saying is that this is a society that knows Majesty exists and furthermore I submit that Kindred society pretty much has to equate supernaturally making someone <i>want</i> to do something the same as actually making them do it, otherwise Majesty is just the socially acceptable version of Dominate (and really -is- overpowered, to tie this back into the original discussion!). How you're supposed to adjudicate cases where that power might or might not have been used and what was done in order to defend oneself from that, well, that's very much up to each domain and who was involved!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resolve. </div> </div> </div>Mea culpa. It's hard to keep track what does what, especially at 3am when I posted that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:47:05-08:00","id":816307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816255#post816255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, the discussion we're having is largely one about design and gameplay, making a mountain of the molehill it usually is in play.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. Usually the most fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correct. If you make the Diplomacy question a binary &quot;yes/no&quot; choice then I fall on the side that says that the PCs can ignore it, because the opposite is that they <i>can't</i>. Rephrased, in situations involving social mechanics, that means that at best what a character does is up to the whims of the dice and at worst the guys with the bigger pools can bully a character into doing something they don't want to or never would do. </div> </div> </div> Well, that's why I do like using the Social Maneuvering, because there's room for saying no, there's room for ignoring the issue, for proposing alternatives. Make no mistake, the system isn't perfect, and we could do with a little more in the system. But the fact that its not binary is one of my favorite aspects of social maneuvering. Too many systems end up with a simple Pass/Fail check on anything social. <br /> <br /> I feel that completely ignoring social rolls and mechanics is just as detrimental as having them used as soft mind control. I think its especially important for social-focused games like Vampire or Beast. Having a binary system is pretty bad. To me, I think that's probably why I focus so much on the Social Manevering system being fine. Because, by default, I see at least four options here - yes, no, propose alternative, ignore (can't open Doors if discussion is never given an opertunity). It allows for much more flexibility than not. It provokes OOC as well as IC discussion. That's my take on the issue. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said that Majesty didn't do anything (at worst, you could argue that I said that Awe is &quot;useless&quot; against PCs) or that it was &quot;blindingly obvious&quot; and that Lashing Out is a given. What I'm saying is that this is a society that knows Majesty exists and furthermore I submit that Kindred society pretty much has to equate supernaturally making someone <i>want</i> to do something the same as actually making them do it, otherwise Majesty is just the socially acceptable version of Dominate (and really -is- overpowered, to tie this back into the original discussion!). </div> </div> </div> Except that goes against what we've heard from the writers. Majesty is supposed to be subtle enough that you can't tell its overtly supernatural, whereas Lashing Out is.<br /> <br /> Does that make it overpowered? I fail to see how. Its part of the nature of the All Night Society. Dominate, Nightmare, Majesty, even Auspex and Obfuscate and Animalism. And lets not forget the Vinculum. Mind control is part of the game. Its part of the built in assumptions. <br /> <br /> I mean, really. Do you want to know something that's actually really horrifying when you think about it? Daeva with Kiss of the Succubus merit. When used on a fellow vampire? Sure, its considered passe to inflict the Kiss. But so what? <i>You're now addicted to the Kiss of the Daeva clan.</i> You're going to come back. They're winning. Seriously. Some of the most scary powerful abilities in the game have nothing to do with statted powers. They're merits. Its like the scariest ability in werewolf isn't turning into a giant death machine, its not Strength or Rage Gifts, or even Catastophe. Its the Efficent Killer merit.<br /> <br /> The power level in 2e has cranked up. That includes mind control being far stronger than before. Its scary, yes, but its not really OP because its part of the baseline. Its the standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:55:56-08:00","id":816314,"title":"","content":"Shifting gears just a little with some advice. Awe used against PCs is a delicate procedure for the Storyteller. As I see it there are two approaches, heavy and light:<ul><li><b>Heavy</b>: This involves rolling dice and informing the player that they should be convinced, or that the vampire they are speaking to must be received positively.</li> <li><b>Light: </b>This approach is wholly narrative and requires the storyteller to constantly describe the NPCs actions in a positive light, lay hints little narrative hints that this NPC is cool/likable/a valuable person to know.</li> </ul>Between the two heavy is a lot easier, but light is far more compelling. Albeit they both depend on how much metagaming your table indulges in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:17:45-08:00","id":816334,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but you're making stuff up about Frenzy. As MCN excellently put it, you spend a point of WP, and you start teh Ride the Wave attempt, which will end in either frenzy or a controlled frenzy. And in any case provocation WILL always be there in any sensible scenario, where a vampire decides he wants to use his WP to enter a frenzy. Maybe just a bit smaller than to trigger unprovocated anger (like, you want to shred someone to pieces easier). <br /> <br /> There's even some fiction with this (tho, it's 1st ed... so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:25:38-08:00","id":816339,"title":"","content":"How can you say I'm making stuff up when I directly quoted the rulebook in multiple locations?<br /> <br /> You can dislike it all you want, but stop claiming I'm making stuff up when I present direct evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:34:28-08:00","id":816345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816339#post816339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you say I'm making stuff up when I directly quoted the rulebook in multiple locations?<br /> <br /> You can dislike it all you want, but stop claiming I'm making stuff up when I present direct evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider both to be possible, since really there's little reason to enter a frenzy without some sort of provocation. The provocation doesn't necessarily have to be enough to require a frenzy check in the first place, but there's something there. You choose to rile yourself up adn risk the frenzy for a reason. That's my reading, anyways. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:43:22-08:00","id":816353,"title":"","content":"I agree with MCN. Beast is always lurking waiting for an excuse to come out and take the control of the vampire. When the vampire want to Ride the Wave, she simply let it free and try to control it. The roll is just to check if the vampire succed to control the beast or fall under its control. This is my interpretation.<br /> The corebook's passages you quoted, in my reading, simply refer to the case where a PC is on the point to lose control and, instead to try to repress the beast, chose to use it on its advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-25-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T14:17:10-08:00","id":816422,"title":"","content":"MCN and Griautis reading is invalidating the entire first dot of coil of the wyrm, that's a pretty clear reason to say it's wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T15:11:34-08:00","id":816452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816422#post816422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MCN and Griautis reading is invalidating the entire first dot of coil of the wyrm, that's a pretty clear reason to say it's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way? Stir the Beast doesn't require any rolls, you just spend the Willpower and Frenzy with your intended goal. It's strictly better than riding the wave under either interpretation,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:05:32-08:00","id":816514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816307#post816307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that goes against what we've heard from the writers. Majesty is supposed to be subtle enough that you can't tell its overtly supernatural, whereas Lashing Out is.<br /> <br /> Does that make it overpowered? I fail to see how. Its part of the nature of the All Night Society. Dominate, Nightmare, Majesty, even Auspex and Obfuscate and Animalism. And lets not forget the Vinculum. Mind control is part of the game. Its part of the built in assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem with mind control. What I have a problem with is the idea that Majesty is so subtle that it's consequence free from both victim and the domain around them. If that's not what you're arguing, great. But what I'm reading is that the rest of Kindred society suddenly forgets that a full clan and an unknown number of bloodlines have mastery of subtle emotion control, and that there's no room for a vampire to become paranoid and act on it with any amount of plausible justification when it comes down to the social checks and balances. To me, the discipline's vaunted &quot;subtlety&quot; only adds [i]more[/;i] paranoia to the All Night Society, not less, and that the social checks and balances take a known quantity of possible mind control into account when it comes to disputes like this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:01:32-08:00","id":816573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty?p=816514#post816514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a problem with mind control. What I have a problem with is the idea that Majesty is so subtle that it's consequence free from both victim and the domain around them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dominate is pretty much &quot;consequence free&quot; by that standard. So are Nightmare and Obfuscate. Majesty should be on par with those when it comes to consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what I'm reading is that the rest of Kindred society suddenly forgets that a full clan and an unknown number of bloodlines have mastery of subtle emotion control, and that there's no room for a vampire to become paranoid and act on it with any amount of plausible justification when it comes down to the social checks and balances. </div> </div> </div> A few problems. One, you don't need a bloodline or be a Daeva to have Majesty. Any vampire can learn it. Two, if you're under the influence of Majesty, you don't feel paranoid or upset on this. Its right there in Charmed Condition - &quot;you don't feel cheated.&quot; &quot;You don't want to believe anything he says is a lie.&quot; Three, Lashing Out just because someone seems attractive is kind of bad form in Elysium, not when you only have <i>suspicions</i>. What if you're wrong? If you want to be paranoid, make an Empathy check with a bonus to see if he's doing something.<br /> <br /> Four, and most importantly, you do feel cheated and upset if some require too much out of you. Majesty is meant to be used subtly, and if you don't? It breaks its hold and becomes worthless. Even Loyalty tends to break if pushed - anyone can spend a point of willpower, make a breaking point check, <i>and resolve the Condition at any point</i>. Think about that. The most powerful effect of Majesty can be pretty much broken at will. Charmed isn't so easily broken, but the favors you ask can't be anything significant or meaningful, or again it snaps. <br /> <br /> In the case of an elder using Charmed to demand a drink? It could arguably a significant enough physical sacrifice to break Charmed if done improperly. That's how weak Majesty is when confronted directly with something you don't want to do.<br /> <br /> No one is suddenly forgetting that Majesty exists. But the simple fact of the matter is that 1) people under the influence don't want to believe they are, and 2) if you use it too forcefully? Majesty breaks. Its subtle because it has to be, or it does nothing. You can't use it as a Dominate replacement; its simply not powerful enough. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't see where people are getting all this brokenness. Dominate is far easier to use and maintain, with far stronger results. Majesty is not easy to pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T22:14:45-08:00","id":816673,"title":"","content":"Imagine Majesty asflirting... Anyone can flirt, and it's usually pretty obvious when someone is flirting with you. And it still feels good... and you (most often) don't lash out and start shouting at the person who's flirting with you.. more often than not, you'll be glad and happy about it. Of course, unless you have some bad experiences with that said person... then him flirting with you might force you to act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}